-    // @orb-waive caught-failure-ownership(visibleLocators): probe-whose-failure-is-its-return-value — a locator failure converts to an empty population and so to pass=false, which the very next line reports as ASSERT visible … FAIL. Ends if that FAIL line stops being printed/read.
-    const matched = await visibleLocators(locator, false).catch((): Locator[] => []);
+    // A locator throw (a selector the engine rejects, a closed page) propagates to `runAssertions`, which prints
+    // the ERROR line: it is a failure to ask, not an absent element.
+    const matched = await visibleLocators(locator, false);

-  // @orb-waive caught-failure-ownership(locator.isVisible): a failed visibility probe is false;
-  // visible/actionable rows require true, while explicit hidden inventory remains locator-only.
+  // @orb-waive caught-failure-ownership(locator.isVisible): a failed probe reads as visible=false, and validateMapEntry skips the candidate of any row whose visibility is "visible"; the row then fails to mint a locator and throws. Ends if validateMapEntry stops checking proof.visible.

-    // @orb-waive caught-failure-ownership(locator.isEnabled): failed enabled proof is false;
-    // a locator-only inventory row can survive it, but an actionable row cannot.
+    // @orb-waive caught-failure-ownership(locator.isEnabled): a failed probe reads as enabled=false, and validateMapEntry skips the candidate of any "actionable" row; the row then fails to mint a locator and throws. Ends if validateMapEntry stops checking proof.enabled.
